<article class="env-lemma" id="0EKA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EKA">Lemma <span data-tag="0EKA">58.24.2</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m)$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $f \in \mathfrak m$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$A$ is $f$-adically complete, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is a nonzerodivisor, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$H^1_\mathfrak m(A/fA)$ and $H^2_\mathfrak m(A/fA)$ are finite $A$-modules, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak p \subset A_ f$ purity holds for $(A_ f)_\mathfrak p$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then the restriction functor $\textit{FÉt}_ U \to \textit{FÉt}_{U_0}$ is essentially surjective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The proof is identical to the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0EK9" data-tag="0EK9">58.24.1</a> using Lemma <a href="/tag/0BLV" data-tag="0BLV">58.23.2</a> in stead of Lemma <a href="/tag/0DXY" data-tag="0DXY">58.23.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>